  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "spring-intake-edu-001",
      "severity": "high",
      "location": {
        "file": "spring-boot/relationships-and-transactions/relationship-pitfalls/topic.json",
        "line": 36
      },
      "claim": "The Fast route has formal prerequisites that occur only after first use: FT3 relationship-pitfalls requires DTOs (FT4) and lazy/eager loading (FT6); FT4 web-layer-tests-with-mockmvc requires ProblemDetail (FT5) and @MockitoBean (FT6); and FT3 spring-data-jpa-with-hibernate requires Flyway (FT4). The intake labels some pages skim/reference or embeds narrower project instruction, but the manifests still define the full later topics as prerequisites, so the canonical Fast path is not honestly teach-before-check.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "file:///Users/jestercharles/.treehouse/pep-technology-content-fb93bc/4/pep-technology-content/curriculum/snapshot/pep-calendar.json",
          "section": "dayTypes and Spring Boot days S1-S13 / FT1-FT8",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-13T13:25:51Z",
          "textSha256": "634da8de5c6034e269b56347b2009fa24eb74eb9bd94f6bd8d5f65f54459ce00"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/reference/testing/mockmvc.html",
          "section": "MockMvc overview and test workflow",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-13T13:23:23Z",
          "textSha256": "1632951727a56f175700a7120c3d0d179e2402b1c958a15fe3a06f29620dd9d7"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Keep the frozen topic order. Distinguish true prerequisites from later enrichment, remove prerequisites that the objective does not need (for example Flyway before introductory JPA), and make each early Fast use self-contained. At FT4, teach and check only the MockMvc behavior available before @MockitoBean/ProblemDetail or provide the minimum just-in-time bridge; at FT3, bridge only the relationship concepts needed for the skim and defer checks that depend on FT4/FT6. Add a track-order prerequisite gate.",
      "reviewedSha256": "91fb8922ab864583f81d0900b2b021d20a2bf1da0bcb555c3c350d9cf0e3a381"
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-intake-edu-002",
      "severity": "high",
      "location": {
        "file": "authoring/evidence/spring-boot/intake.md",
        "line": 375
      },
      "claim": "The S6, FT5 and FT7 project plans apply their central outcomes before those outcomes have been taught on a prior route segment. S6 teaches layers, DTOs and pagination inside its Build block; FT5 teaches validation/error handling inside its 85-minute implementation block; FT7 does the same for password hashing, JWTs, authorization and the dev profile. Calling an embedded teach/check immediately before each coding step is useful scaffolding, but it does not meet the intake requirement that every applied project concept be taught before the project begins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "file:///Users/jestercharles/.treehouse/pep-technology-content-fb93bc/4/pep-technology-content/curriculum/snapshot/pep-calendar.json",
          "section": "dayTypes and Spring Boot days S1-S13 / FT1-FT8",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-13T13:25:51Z",
          "textSha256": "634da8de5c6034e269b56347b2009fa24eb74eb9bd94f6bd8d5f65f54459ce00"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.cmu.edu/teaching/designteach/design/learningobjectives.html",
          "section": "Articulate Your Learning Objectives — alignment, measurable objectives, and assessment",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-13T13:25:51Z",
          "textSha256": "dfbb33d7a75a83ce7b896245c1805bb4f9cda084386a091699ff2e886b566fcd"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Preserve the syllabus and project rows, but put the canonical instruction and a successful check before learners open each project scaffold. The Standard S6 route should complete the three S6 instructional pages/checks before the Build block; Fast FT5/FT7 should use an explicit pre-implementation teaching/diagnostic phase before project work, with the build reserved for transfer and feedback. Keep embedded reminders, but do not count them as prior teaching.",
      "reviewedSha256": "b2521d00cae0420b9fa9d40eb644b00bc0a19966fbb0b9f22fd8f9932aa59934"
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-intake-edu-003",
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": {
        "file": "authoring/evidence/spring-boot/intake.md",
        "line": 416
      },
      "claim": "The six cumulative Fast increments are detailed only in intake prose while their repository slot remains open and course.json keeps courseLabs empty. Consequently, no manifest currently binds increment order, scaffold/extension identity, public-test packages, claimed-versus-practised fragments or the 70-minute budgets; later module authors could implement incompatible pieces while all topic manifests remain valid.",
